\import{base-macros}
\author{kellenkanarios}
\title{First-order optimality condition}
\taxon{Theorem}
\tag{public}

\p{If #{\mathbf{x_\star}} is a local minimizer of #{f:\mathbb{R}^n\to\mathbb{R}} and #{f} is continuously differentiable in an open neighborhood of #{\mathbf{x_\star}}, then #{\mathbf{x_\star}} is a [stationary point](003P):
##{\nabla f(\mathbf{x_\star})\ =\ \mathbf{0}.}}

\p{This is only \em{necessary}: a stationary point may be a maximizer or saddle, which is what the [second-order conditions](U3L4) disambiguate. Under [convexity](004D) it becomes sufficient as well — a stationary point of a convex function is a global minimizer.}
